u$ is called *stable* if all of its solutions are bounded on $\mathbb{R}$ ; otherwise the equation is called *unstable* . If $
u$ is not an integer, then ( 29.2.1 ) is unstable iff $h\leq a^{0}_{
u}\left(k^{2}ight)$ or $h$ lies in one of the closed intervals with endpoints $a^{m}_{
u}\left(k^{2}ight)$ and $b^{m}_{
u}\left(k^{2}ight)$ , $m=1,2,\dots$ . If $
u$ is a nonnegative integer, then ( 29.2.1 ) is unstable iff $h\leq a^{0}_{
u}\left(k^{2}ight)$ or $h\in[b^{m}_{
u}\left(k^{2}ight),a^{m}_{
u}\left(k^{2}ight)]$ for some $m=1,2,\dots,
u$ .

